course: dictionary
lesson: 5492
title: The word laughter
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Laughter is the sound or the act of laughing. It is a noun, and it is a word we do not count. You cannot have two laughters, but you can hear a lot of laughter. Look at this: «Then he hears loud laughter: she has been watching him all along.» The word laughter tells you what he hears.
explain: The words around laughter give it its strength. «Alice gives a little scream of laughter» means a small, sudden laugh. Phrases like «burst into laughter» and «roars of laughter» show a much bigger laugh, and «full of laughter» tells you a person or a place is happy and noisy with it.
explain: Laughter can be kind or unkind. «Laughter can be friendly, not mean; people often like you more if you can laugh at yourself.» Laughing with someone shares the fun. Laughing at someone can hurt them. Read the clues to find out which kind is happening.
fact: Laughter is the sound or act of laughing.
fact: Laughter is a noun, and it is uncountable: we say some laughter, not two laughters.
fact: «Burst into laughter» means to suddenly start laughing.
fact: «Roars of laughter» means very loud, strong laughing.
fact: «Laughter lines» is a kind name for the wrinkles around the eyes and mouth that appear when people laugh a lot.
exercise: «Then he hears loud laughter: she has been watching him all along.» What is laughter? | A type of sweet food | A quiet, serious look | A kind of loud shout for help | *The sound or act of laughing
exercise: «Alice gives a little scream of laughter.» Is this laughter loud or small? | Very loud, like roars | Never heard before | Silent and still | *Small, a little sudden burst
exercise: «Laughter lines» is a kind name for what? | Scars on the knees | Dimples on the chin | Freckles on the nose | *Wrinkles around the eyes and mouth
test: What does the phrase «burst into laughter» mean? | Slowly stopped talking | Ran out of the room | *Suddenly started laughing | Fell fast asleep
test: Laughter is good for mood and helps people feel what? | Angry and quiet | Tired and cold | Hungry and lost | *Happier and closer to each other
exam: Which sentence uses laughter correctly? | *The room was full of laughter. | The laughter were loud. | The room laughtered loudly. | She laughters a lot, two times.
